      "commit_id": null,
      "commit_url": null,
      "created_at": "2026-09-02T15:17:24Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-02T15:17:24Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "This `m_best_header` [assert](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/b811aeabad94ef48cd0f0fb1d2fcc456594aeedb/src/validation.cpp#L5175) in `CheckBlockIndex` can be hit if an invalid block is given while an `InvalidateBlock` is happening:\n- The loop to populate `highpow_outofchain_headers` only considers valid headers, this runs [here](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/b811aeabad94ef48cd0f0fb1d2fcc456594aeedb/src/validation.cpp#L3552-L3567)\n- If we receive the block (via p2p/rpc) for a header in this multimap and it happens to be invalid, the check that may update `m_best_header` to one of these candidates headers does not then check if the candidate was marked invalid in the meantime [here](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/b811aeabad94ef48cd0f0fb1d2fcc456594aeedb/src/validation.cpp#L3641-L3644).\n- This may update `m_best_header` to an invalid block\n\nThis `CheckBlockIndex` [assert](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/b811aeabad94ef48cd0f0fb1d2fcc456594aeedb/src/validation.cpp#L5292) can be hit if `reconsiderblock` runs at the same time as `invalidateblock`:\n- the main loop will lock cs_main, mark disconnected blocks (and things in the candidate set) as `BLOCK_FAILED_VALID`, and release cs_main\n- `ReconsiderBlock` will lock cs_main and may call `ResetBlockFailureFlags` on one of those blocks [here](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/b811aeabad94ef48cd0f0fb1d2fcc456594aeedb/src/rpc/blockchain.cpp#L1777)\n- the disconnect loop continues to run\n- the assert is hit because there are valid blocks descending from invalid blocks\n\nVibe-coded reproducers for these two issues [here](https://github.com/Crypt-iQ/bitcoin/tree/09022026/invalidate_block_rpc_tests). The first issue could be fixed by checking that the candidates are valid before updating `m_best_header`. The second issue could be fixed by preventing `reconsiderblock` from competing with `invalidateblock` via a dedicated mutex or perhaps by moving the `CheckBlockIndex` call after the `InvalidChainFound` [here](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/b811aeabad94ef48cd0f0fb1d2fcc456594aeedb/src/validation.cpp#L3681)?",
